From b18327ab23ac2c23d46b362ba485d9262fe2b962 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vpestininkas <159783366+Vpestininkas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:20:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] config: ipu7x: imx471: do not flip the sensor vertically

The ipu7x IMX471 config sets V4L2_CID_VFLIP to 1 while declaring the
sensor and CSI-2 receiver formats as SRGGB10. The in-tree imx471 driver
(drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c) reports the Bayer order that follows from
its flip controls, so with VFLIP set the sensor pad is SGBRG10, link
validation fails and VIDIOC_STREAMON on the ISYS capture node returns
EPIPE ("Broken pipe"); the camera never delivers a frame.

With both flips off the sensor reports SRGGB10, matching the config and
the static graph. The ipu75xa IMX471 config already uses VFLIP 0. The
sensor reports camera_sensor_rotation = 180, so consumers that rotate
by that (as v4l2-relayd's videoflip method=rotate-180 does) get an
upright picture.

Tested on a Lenovo ThinkPad X9-15 Gen 1 (Lunar Lake, IPU 8086:645d,
SONY471A) with linux 7.2.15.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 config/linux/ipu7x/sensors/imx471-uf.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/config/linux/ipu7x/sensors/imx471-uf.json b/config/linux/ipu7x/sensors/imx471-uf.json
index 4ee332d..4aaebda 100644
--- a/config/linux/ipu7x/sensors/imx471-uf.json
+++ b/config/linux/ipu7x/sensors/imx471-uf.json
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
                 "name": "imx471 $I2CBUS", "ctrlId": "V4L2_CID_HFLIP", "value": 0
               },
               {
-                "name": "imx471 $I2CBUS", "ctrlId": "V4L2_CID_VFLIP", "value": 1
+                "name": "imx471 $I2CBUS", "ctrlId": "V4L2_CID_VFLIP", "value": 0
               },
 	    ],
             "videonode": [
